<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs fall in week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe fell by three to 54 in the week to September 25, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The U.K. sector fell by four rigs to 27 rigs active while Norwegian activity increased by one rig to 14.</p>
<p>Dutch rig counts rose by two rigs to nine active while the Danish sector was down one at three and Irish activity was unchanged at one.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity was up two at five rigs, four in the U.K. and one in the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
